I appoint my wife, Sunita Mehra, as the Executor of this my Will. In the event that Sunita Mehra is unable or unwilling to act, or having begun to act is unable or unwilling to continue to act, as Executor, whether by reason of death, incapacity, renunciation or otherwise, I appoint my daughter, Riya Mehra, as the alternate Executor of this my Will.

I direct that my Executor shall have the following powers, to be exercised at the Executor's discretion for the due administration of my estate:

(a) to collect, get in and take possession of all assets comprised in my estate;

(b) to pay all debts, funeral expenses, taxes and testamentary expenses as directed above;

(c) to sell, call in, convert into money or otherwise realise any part of my estate to the extent reasonably necessary for the payment of debts, taxes and testamentary expenses, or for effecting distribution among the beneficiaries;

(d) to distribute the assets of my estate in specie among the beneficiaries entitled thereto under this Will, at such values as the Executor considers fair and reasonable;

(e) to take all steps necessary to apply for and obtain probate of this Will, or such other grant of representation as may be required in law;

(f) to do all other acts, deeds and things as may be necessary or expedient for the due administration and distribution of my estate in accordance with this Will.

My Executor shall not be liable for any loss to my estate arising from any act done or omitted to be done in good faith in the honest exercise of the powers and discretions conferred by this Will, but nothing in this clause shall exonerate my Executor from liability for any act done in bad faith, wilful default or gross negligence.
